From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone-1.2: USB-C host or peripheral

The ANX7688 linked to the USB PHY's role switch (0042), as in Megi's
tree: the data role it negotiates routes the port to MUSB (a peripheral
to a computer: the console, the network, updates) or to EHCI0/OHCI0,
enabled again for it (0002 had them off: unclaimed, they took the port),
the host of a dock's hub, a mouse or a keyboard.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone-1.2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone-1.2.dts
@@ -151,6 +151,13 @@
 		 */
 		vbus-supply = <&reg_usb_5v>;
 		vbus_in-supply = <&usb_power_supply>;
+
+		/* The data role it negotiates switches the port: host (a dock, a keyboard) or not */
+		port {
+			typec0_dr_sw: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usb0_drd_sw>;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 };
 
@@ -190,3 +197,31 @@
 		remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_con_in>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The USB-C port either way, as the ANX7688 negotiates its data role (its port, and the
+ * PHY a role switch: Megi's): a peripheral to a computer (MUSB, the gadget), the host
+ * of a dock's hub or a keyboard (EHCI0/OHCI0, which the dtsi leaves off: probed without
+ * a role claimed, they took the port from the gadget, 0002-…).
+ */
+&usb_otg {
+	dr_mode = "otg";
+};
+
+&usbphy {
+	usb-role-switch;
+
+	port {
+		usb0_drd_sw: endpoint {
+			remote-endpoint = <&typec0_dr_sw>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&ehci0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ohci0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
